SF Crafting Essentials combines recipe-cost changes, supported item-use changes, and production-time controls in one ShroudForge package. Its package ID is <code>sf-crafting-essentials</code>. It targets the client and Dedicated Server, requests the <code>patch</code> and <code>runtime</code> capabilities, and is disabled by default.

== Settings ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Setting !! Default !! Activation !! Effect and limits
|-
| No Recipe Resource Costs || Off || Startup asset preparation. Restart required. || Sets direct recipe ingredients, category ingredients, and water charges to zero. Building costs, upgrade costs, and other shared inventory costs are unchanged.
|-
| No Item Consumption || Off || Live. || Prevents supported item-use actions from consuming food, potions, bandages, and other covered items. Some actions are not supported. Recipe ingredients, trades, and inventory transfers are unchanged.
|-
| Recipe Time Mode || Original recipe times || Restart required to change mode. || Choose between live proportional scaling of original recipe times and one shared duration for all timed recipes.
|-
| Production Time in Seconds || 3 seconds || Startup asset preparation in shared-time mode. Restart required. || Sets every positive timed recipe to the selected base duration. Range: 1–900 seconds. Instant recipes and output quantities are unchanged.
|-
| Production Duration Scale || 100% || Live in original-time mode. || Scales loaded timed recipes proportionally. At 0%, the shortest timed recipe takes 1 second and other recipes retain their relative times. At 100%, original recipe durations are restored.
|}

== Recipe costs ==

No Recipe Resource Costs changes recipe data during startup asset preparation, before Enshrouded loads production stations. It covers direct ingredients, category ingredients, and water charges stored on recipes. It does not remove building or upgrade costs, or other inventory costs. The change requires a restart.

The setting applies to matching recipes as a group. It does not provide a per-recipe selector. Changing costs during an active production order could also affect its refund, so the mod applies the change before normal gameplay.

== Item use ==

No Item Consumption changes supported loaded item-use actions while the game is running. It changes only covered consume fields that were originally enabled. The scan runs incrementally to avoid blocking a game update. Action sequences may be shared by several actors, so the result can affect other actors that use the same sequence.

This feature does not cover every item or transaction. It does not change recipe ingredients, trades, inventory transfers, or unsupported item actions. The current game capture has 2,157 action-sequence resources and 4,262 ItemInfo records. Those are distinct resource counts, not a claim that every item is covered.

== Production time ==

In '''Original recipe times''' mode, each recipe keeps its own duration as a baseline. The live scale adjusts every timed recipe by the same ratio and preserves their relative durations. At 0%, the shortest timed recipe becomes 1 second. At 100%, original durations are restored. The mod leaves the world's production-speed factor unchanged. Changes can affect production already in progress.

In '''One shared time for all recipes''' mode, startup preparation gives every timed recipe the selected base duration. The seconds control is available only in this mode. The live scale is available only in Original recipe times mode. Changing the mode or shared duration requires a restart.

== Technical scope ==

The package uses the <code>patch</code> capability for pregame recipe-data changes and the <code>runtime</code> capability for typed live operations. It does not install executable hooks or write game code.

Inventory splitting is not included as a setting. The current public runtime API does not provide safe access to the live inventory transaction at the moment the game removes the source quantity. That feature needs a verified native transaction operation.

